    <enigmaLogo place="above"/>
  </cover>
  <contents>
    <enigmaLogo/>
  </contents>
  <chapter name="introduction" columns="1" credit="Test Author">
    <chapterTitle>Where the River Splits</chapterTitle>
    <section name="intro-opening">
      <p>Travellers on the <nounRef ref="copperway" value="name"/> reach <nounRef ref="grand-forks" value="name"/> after three days of empty road, and the Tollwarden meets them at the bridge.</p>
      <speakAloud>
        <trigger>When the party first sees the town:</trigger>
        <p>The road crests a low hill, and below you the river splits in two around a town built on three banks.</p>
      </speakAloud>
      <p><nounRef ref="grand-forks" value="name"/> sits where the <nounRef ref="river-sallow" value="name"/> splits around a wedge of high ground. The <nounRef ref="river-sallow" value="shortName"/> is slow and brown, and the <nounRef ref="river-sallow" value="shortName"/> turns every mill in town. Swimmers who fight the current end up <condition>restrained</condition> unless they pass <skillcheck stat="str" skill="athletics" dc="13"/>; the chapter on <chapterRef name="tollside"/> has the fines.</p>
      <figure id="fig-town-map" name="Grand Forks and the Sallow">
        <image id="img-map" span="both"/>
      </figure>
      <p><figureRef ref="fig-town-map"/> shows all three pieces.</p>
    </section>
    <section name="three-pieces">
      <title>The Three Pieces</title>
      <p>Each piece still keeps its own customs.</p>
      <p>The town is really three towns:</p>
      <list bullet="number">
        <li>Tollside, on the north bank, where the road arrives.</li>
        <li>Millward, on the east fork.</li>
        <li>The Wedge, on the high ground between.</li>
      </list>
    </section>
  </chapter>
  <chapter name="tollside">
    <chapterTitle>Tollside</chapterTitle>
    <section name="toll-bridge">
      <title>The Toll Bridge</title>
      <p>Every traveller pays the toll of <dataRef ref="bridgeToll" value="value"/> at the north end of the bridge.</p>
      <tableLink id="toll-rates"/>
      <image id="img-toll-bridge" placement="top"/>
      <parcelLink number="1"/>
    </section>
    <section name="coaching-inn">
      <title>The Copper Kettle Inn</title>
      <p>The Copper Kettle is where the toll disputes end up.</p>
      <sidebarLink id="toll-disputes"/>
    </section>
    <section name="wardens-house">
      <title>The Warden's House</title>
      <p>The Toll Warden lives above the gatehouse.</p>
      <dialog speaker="Toll Warden">
        <trigger>If a traveller argues about the toll:</trigger>
        <p>Two coppers, friend. The river does not cross itself.</p>
        <p>And no, the Sallow does not count as a road.</p>
      </dialog>
    </section>
    <table id="toll-rates">
      <title>Bridge Tolls</title>
      <header>
        <th>Traveller</th>
        <th>Toll</th>
        <th>Notes</th>
      </header>
      <tableBody>
        <tr>
          <td>On foot</td>
          <td>
            <dataRef ref="bridgeToll" value="value"/>
          </td>
          <td>Children cross free</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Cart or wagon</td>
          <td>5 cp</td>
          <td>Per axle</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Herd animals</td>
          <td>1 cp a head</td>
          <td>The warden counts them</td>
        </tr>
      </tableBody>
    </table>
    <sidebar id="toll-disputes">
      <title>Toll Disputes</title>
      <p>A traveller who will not pay is held until the Toll Warden hears the case.</p>
    </sidebar>
  </chapter>
  <chapter name="millward">
    <chapterTitle>Millward</chapterTitle>
    <section name="weir">
      <title>The Weir</title>
      <p>Below the weir lives a <monsterRef ref="forkjaw-pike" value="name"/>, and the stones are slick. Crossing on foot takes <skillcheck stat="dex" skill="acrobatics" dc="13" table="true"/>; a slip means <hazard name="falling">a fall</hazard>.</p>
      <skillcheckResultTable stat="dex" skill="acrobatics">
        <result dc="10">
          <rd>You keep your feet, barely.</rd>
        </result>
        <result dc="15">
          <rd>You cross without getting wet.</rd>
        </result>
      </skillcheckResultTable>
    </section>
    <section name="mills">
      <title>The Mills</title>
      <p>A miller caught in the race makes <savingthrow stat="str" dc="12"/> or is pulled under the wheel.</p>
    </section>
    <section name="pike-attack">
      <title>Trouble in the Water</title>
      <p>The pike attacks anyone who swims out to the matriarch’s pool.</p>
      <monsterEntry ref="forkjaw-pike" omit="quoteBox" omitParts="pike-lore">
            </monsterEntry>
      <parcelLink number="2"/>
    </section>
  </chapter>
  <chapter name="wedge">
    <chapterTitle>The Wedge</chapterTitle>
    <section name="market">
      <title>Wedge Market</title>
      <p>Ferry hands sell a <itemRef ref="ferrymans-lantern" value="name"/> to anyone crossing after dark.</p>
      <magicItemBlock ref="ferrymans-lantern"/>
      <image id="img-lantern"/>
      <figure id="fig-bridge-again" name="The bridge from the market">
        <image id="img-toll-bridge"/>
      </figure>
      <pageEnd balance="false"/>
    </section>
    <section name="ferry-shrine">
      <title>The Ferry Shrine</title>
      <p>The shrine’s keeper teaches <spellRef ref="fork-the-current" value="name"/> to ferry hands.</p>
      <spellBlock ref="fork-the-current"/>
    </section>
  </chapter>
  <chapter name="creatures" kind="appendix">
    <chapterTitle>Creatures of the Forks</chapterTitle>
    <section name="creatures">
      <title>Creatures</title>
      <p>The <monsterRef ref="toll-warden" value="name"/> keeps order; a <monsterRef ref="bandit" value="name"/> or two works the road; the <monsterRef ref="pike-spirit" value="name"/> haunts the weir.</p>
      <monsterStatblock ref="toll-warden"/>
      <monsterStatblock ref="bandit"/>
    </section>
  </chapter>
